                "rationale": "Prairie-dog die-offs are the canonical sentinel — the colonies collapse 2–4 weeks before human cases appear in adjacent communities. Sick or dead cats in northern AZ are an even stronger personal-exposure signal: feline plague has a 50% case-fatality-rate untreated, and approximately one-third of cat-associated human cases occur in veterinarians and household members of the cat."
            },
            "az_geography": ["Coconino", "Apache", "Navajo"],
            "person_to_person": "pneumonic only"
